ords and some of them sounded like “Valha” in Marathi, which means oars", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-13T00:15:01Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "the word i have in mind is: Tamil paṭavu, Telugu paḍava, and Kannada haDagu", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-13T00:15:12Z", "username": "Dr.Namrata Srinivasan", "text": "Makes sense", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-13T00:15:18Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "the most common word in Telugu for boat is paDava", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-13T00:15:29Z", "username": "Dr.Namrata Srinivasan", "text": "Boats are not referred to as kappal usually I think", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-13T00:15:42Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Sanskrit pATava, Marathi paḍāṃva, Konkani paḍāva, Gujarati padavo, Odia padhua, Sinhala paruwa", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-13T00:15:58Z", "username": "Khandoba", "text": "I think the more appropriate Marathi word is “hodi”", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-13T00:16:01Z", "username": "Khandoba", "text": "For a boat", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-13T00:16:50Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Yeah I don’t speak Tamil but what I have read is that kappal is used for vessel/ship", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-13T00:19:12Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "This is what sent me down this rabbit hole ‎<attached: 00114083-PHOTO-2026-04-12-17-19-12.j